Perfect. I'll use exactly these column names in your existing Oracle 11g `INFO` table:

| Column       | Purpose           |
| ------------ | ----------------- |
| `EMP_ID`     | Employee ID       |
| `FULL_NAME`  | Employee name     |
| `DEPARTMENT` | Department        |
| `POSITION`   | Job position      |
| `JOIN_DATE`  | Joining date      |
| `SALARY`     | Salary            |
| `PERF_SCORE` | Performance score |
| `OFFICE_LOC` | Office location   |

I'll build the application for JDK 1.6 + Tomcat 6 + Oracle 11g, using JSP, Servlets and JDBC. The dashboard will retrieve employee records and counts directly from your database.

