Add `ojdbc6.jar` to your project's `WEB-INF/lib` folder. It is the Oracle JDBC driver suitable for Java 6.

## 2. Database connection – DBConnection.java

Change the database username, password and SID to match your Oracle installation.

```

package com.ems;

import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;

public class DBConnection {

    private static final String URL =
        "jdbc:oracle:thin:@localhost:1521:XE";

    private static final String USER = "system";
    private static final String PASSWORD = "your_password";

    public static Connection getConnection() throws Exception {

        Class.forName("oracle.jdbc.driver.OracleDriver");

        Connection con = DriverManager.getConnection(
            URL, USER, PASSWORD
        );

        return con;
    }
}

